				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				7
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates delivering Vine notification stream and development build config\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\n- Wind (274df239): Add Vine notification stream service. Implement `VineNotifications` and `VineNotificationsLive` — an Effect-TS Layer that bridges Mountain's process-wide Vine notification broadcast to a `Stream<NotificationFrame>` consumable by Wind/Sky subscribers. The Layer opens a Tauri channel via `vine_subscribe_notifications` command, draining the Mountain broadcast receiver into an unbounded Effect Queue. Adds convenience functions for filtering (`SubscribeMethodPrefix`, `SubscribeMethod`) and diagnostic query (`SubscriberCount`). This completes P14.5 notification subscription surface.\n\n- Mountain (0a0e22ba): Update binary/lib names and Tauri config for development build profile. Rename the Mountain binary and library to include the full development environment profile string to distinguish this build variant from production builds. Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier, add Binary/node to externalBin.\n\n- Output (c97cc8b1): Extract polyfill bodies to type-checked modules. Move inline polyfill IIFE bodies from Transform/*.ts to new Polyfill/*.ts modules enabling compile-time type-checking and tree-shaking. Add 4 new Inject* transforms, 3 new Replace* transforms (ReplaceTelemetryService, ReplaceUpdateService, ReplaceExtensionGalleryService) that replace VS Code services with no-op stubs. New boot-time behaviors: InjectStripBackgroundPolling, InjectEagerLifecyclePhase, InjectEagerExtensionActivation, InjectEagerIdleValue.\n\n- Rest (9c003845): Rebuild Rest binary following CHANGELOG overhaul.\n\n- Cocoon, Echo, Sky: Submodule pointer updates.",
			"SHA": "3ef0e05b6ff28605c5fa9b868f14c9790bf06c37"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T01:35:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Vine notification subscription for Sky/Wind\n\nAdd `VineSubscribeCommand` Tauri command surface exposing process-wide Vine notification broadcast to Sky/Wind via `Channel<NotificationFramePayload>`. This enables the frontend to subscribe to notifications from Cocoon with the same ordering and drop-oldest semantics as in-process Rust subscribers. Effect-TS layer wraps this into a `Stream<NotificationFrame>`.\n\nAlso add conditional streaming multiplexer support in `Vine::Client` for both `SendRequest` and `SendNotification` when `LAND_VINE_STREAMING=1` is set. The multiplexer path attempts h2-multiplexed streaming and falls back to unary path on any failure, ensuring the editor remains functional while Cocoon's streaming handler tree lands.\n\nThis completes the P14.x notification subscription surface, complementing the P14.3/P14.2 multiplexer integration in Client.rs.",
			"SHA": "f120a534ca369fcb13edb307afb488364eec9a52"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T01:24:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates delivering B7-S6 infrastructure foundations\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\n- Mist (9998d872): Implement WebSocket transport for Sky↔Cocoon direct path. Add new WebSocket module for local-first JSON-RPC, removing Tauri-invoke → Mountain-gRPC double hop (~95% of IPC volume). Includes ServeLocal TCP listener, Client with background reader, X-Land-Secret auth, exponential backoff reconnect. This is the B7-S6 P1.1 foundation for direct extension-API communication.\n\n- Mountain (87bdf4c0): Implement mmap asset cache, path canon cache, and Vine streaming foundation (B7-S6 P2). AssetMemoryMap.rs provides file-backed mmap cache for ~80MB of bundled assets eliminating per-request read(2) duplication. PathCanon.rs adds process-wide canonical path cache with 60s TTL saving ~150ms boot time. Vine/Multiplexer.rs adds Envelope protobuf and OpenChannel streaming RPCs. Also integrates Air sidecar, fixes MIME-honesty on 404, and serves Brotli precompressed assets.\n\n- Output (13d8a561): Add Network/ChromiumIPC excludes stripping dead code (~25KB reduction), WKWebView lazy-paint fixes via four new transforms: InjectDisableLazyPaint (rAF→setTimeout), InjectWorkbenchInteractivityCSS (force pointer-events), InjectWorkbenchPaintPrime (offsetHeight reads), InjectTelemetryConsentOff (pre-baked telemetry off). Also fixes GPU layer CSS to scope contain:paint to canvas only.\n\n- Sky (2d34bedf): Bump zod 4.3.6→4.4.0, @xterm/xterm 6.1.0-beta.204→207. Fix Bundled variant build by converting static Astro imports to dynamic await import() to avoid walking unmangled gulp-only module graph. Add BundledEntryStubInactive Vite plugin to short-circuit inactive variants. Includes auto-generated SkyChannels.ts documenting 59 sky:// IPC channels.\n\nThis synchronization lands core B7-S6 infrastructure: direct WebSocket path, memory-mapped caching, streaming foundation, and WKWebView rendering fixes.",
			"SHA": "dedc1e48e10ab8cbffe0ff0362bf9694488c8ce2"
		}
	],
